Someone set up a raised bed and a pile of different vegetable starters; now they need to pick which ones to plant so the projected harvest is as valuable as possible. The plan is to choose a selection of distinct seedlings, compute the garden's projected haul by adding each chosen seedling's expected value, and keep the combined soil volume of those seedlings under the bed's capacity - no duplicates and no half-plants. The concrete data about varieties, volumes, and expected yields follows below.

